  - "Ragi flour - 1/3 cup"
  - "Carrot - 1 small size"
  - "Bengal gram flour - 3 tsp"
  - "Onion - 1 small size"
  - "Capsicum - 1 small size"
  - "Cabbage - 4 small leaves"
  - "Oil - 1 tbsp"
  - "Coriander leaves - Few"
  - "Ginger paste - ½ tsp"
  - "Water - 150 ml (approx.)"
instructions:
  - "Chop vegetables and blanch for five minutes."
  - "Mix ragi, Bengal gram flour, salt, and green chili to make a batter by adding water."
  - "Heat oil, add green chilies and chopped onion, stir-fry till transparent. Add blanched vegetables and stir-fry for 5 minutes with the lid on."
  - "Add coriander leaves to the fried vegetables."
  - "Divide the fried vegetables into six equal portions."
  - "Heat a tawa, grease it with oil, put a ladleful of batter, and spread it."
  - "Cook for a few seconds and turn the side."
  - "Spread a portion of fried vegetables over it."
  - "Cook for a few seconds, roll it, and serve with chutney."
